  <section id="protocol" class="wrap section-sm" aria-label="Change protocol">
    <h2><span class="mono"># </span>Change protocol</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Every stream connection opens with one synthesized
      <span class="mono">hello</span> frame — no SSE id, never stored, never
      acknowledged — carrying <span class="mono">{'{ apiVersion, chainId, processor, coverage }'}</span>
      as of your resume position. Change events follow, at-least-once;
      consumers dedupe by cursor. Every event also records its processing origin
      and publication revision. Exactly-once lives in an atomic application
      commit followed by acknowledgement, not in the transport.
    </p>
    <TerminalFrame title="stream — wire format">
      <span class="t-line t-dim">GET /v1/processors/blobs-money/stream?after=&lt;cursor&gt;</span>
      <span class="t-line t-accent">event: hello</span>
      <span class="t-line">data: {'{"apiVersion":"1","chainId":1,"processor":{…},"coverage":{…}}'}</span>
      <span class="t-line"></span>
      <span class="t-line t-dim">id: &lt;opaque cursor&gt;</span>
      <span class="t-line t-accent">event: apply</span>
      <span class="t-line">data: {'{"kind":"blobs.block.put",…,"data":{…}}'}</span>
    </TerminalFrame>
    <h3 class="mono">envelope</h3>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{envelopeFields.map(([f, t, d]) => (
          <tr><td class="mono">{f}</td><td class="mono type">{t}</td><td>{d}</td></tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="json-rpc" class="wrap section-sm" aria-label="JSON-RPC">
    <h2><span class="mono"># </span>JSON-RPC subset</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The capability response is authoritative. Number/range history can use a
      configured complete source; hash-only history is recent-only unless a
      locator or retained index is enabled. Unavailable material returns an
      explicit data-unavailable error instead of a fabricated null result.
    </p>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="panel ok">
        <h3 class="mono ok-h">implemented exactly when available</h3>
        <ul class="mono list">{rpcServed.map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3 class="mono no-h">refused, explicitly</h3>
        <ul class="mono list dead">{rpcRefused.map((m) => <li>{m}</li>)}</ul>
        <p class="note-p">No EVM, no state trie. Unsupported methods return an explicit error. <a href="/#rpc">Why →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

