    <h3 class="mono">helpers</h3>
    <div class="scroll"><table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Function</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{sdkHelpers.map(([c, r]) => (
        <tr><td class="mono">{c}</td><td>{r}</td></tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h3 class="mono">@leani/sdk/backfill</h3>
    <p class="note-p">
      The separate backfill entry point owns bounded historical subscriptions,
      gzip NDJSON batch decoding, lane-specific acknowledgements, and a unified
      history-to-live handoff. Import it explicitly so browser/query clients do
      not pay for delivery orchestration they do not use.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll"><table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Call</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{sdkBackfill.map(([c, r]) => (
        <tr><td class="mono">{c}</td><td>{r}</td></tr>
      ))}</tbody>
    </table></div>

    <p class="note-p">
      Errors are <span class="mono">LeaniError</span> (status, code, retryable,
      requestId); an unresumable cursor throws
      <span class="mono">ResetRequiredError</span>. Streams reconnect with
      backoff and jitter, resume from the last yielded cursor, and surface each
      connection's <span class="mono">hello</span> via
      <span class="mono">onHello</span>.
    </p>
    <p class="note-p">
      Browser use requires same-origin deployment or an application-owned
      reverse proxy with explicit CORS. Never place a privileged admin bearer
      token in browser code.
    </p>
